Non-primitive types

TP                  lit-time            ietf-yang-types:date-and-time OR
                                        amm:date-and-time with normative text

TD                  lit-time            typedef amm:duration {
                                            type string {
                                                pattern "P(?=.*[YMWDTHS])(?:\d+Y)?(?:\d+M)?(?:\d+W)?(?:\d+D)?(?:T(?:\d+H)?(?:\d+M)?(?:\d+S)?)?";
                                                reference "RFC 3339";
                                            }
                                        }

                                        Should this really be allowed to be pos/neg?
                                        How is a duration negative?

LABEL               lit-label           typedef amm:label {
                                            type string { pattern "[A-Za-z].*"; }
                                        }

CBOR                lit-cbor            typedef amm:cbor {
                                            type binary;
                                        }


